ers call the contest Likely or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Jones roughly a one-in-six chance of winning.\n\nStill, the race has drawn unusual attention. Two polls, including a Hendrix College survey in August, showed Jones narrowly ahead, and a favorable national environment plus endorsements from Kamala Harris and Joe Kennedy III have raised his profile. A Republican complaint over a missing financial disclosure complicates his campaign. The balance of evidence keeps Hill favored by mid-single digits, with genuine room for movement if newer surveys confirm the earlier ones.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1835, "margin": -5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.3532, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.3233, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2423, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.2933, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.1983, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.3205, "margin": -3.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.3445, "margin": -3.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.2683, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.2665, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.2648, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.2693, "margin": -4.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.2035, "margin": -5.5}]}